// ============================================================================
// card-draw-probabilities.epher -- two draws from a deck, two methods
//
// Drawing two cards without replacement makes the second draw depend on
// the first, so probabilities can be counted two equivalent ways: with
// combinations, which count the unordered hands directly, or with
// conditional products, which multiply along the draws,
//
//   P(ace then ace) = (4/52) * (3/51)
//   P(heart then spade) = (13/52) * (13/51)
//
// The heart-then-spade probability is slightly larger than the
// with-replacement value (13/52)^2 = 1/16 = 0.0625, because taking a
// heart out of the deck leaves 51 cards with all 13 spades still in
// them: 13/51 > 13/52.
//
// Source: Feller, "An Introduction to Probability Theory and Its
// Applications", volume 1, chapter 1. All fractions are exact.
//
// Run it from a terminal:  epher "epher scripts/probability/games/card-draw-probabilities.epher"
// Web/desktop:             paste the file into the entry, press Enter
// ============================================================================

// ---- results ----
// Two aces in two draws: combinations count the 6 ace pairs among all
// ncr(52, 2) = 1326 hands; the conditional product multiplies 4/52 by
// the 3/51 chance of a second ace once one is gone.
print("ncr count: ncr(4, 2) / ncr(52, 2) =", ncr(4, 2) / ncr(52, 2))
print("product: (4/52) * (3/51) =", (4/52) * (3/51))
(4/52) * (3/51) == ncr(4, 2) / ncr(52, 2)

// Heart then spade, in that order: 13 hearts first, then one of the 13
// spades among the 51 remaining cards.
print("ordered count: (13 * 13) / (52 * 51) =", (13 * 13) / (52 * 51))
print("product: (13/52) * (13/51) =", (13/52) * (13/51))

// The with-replacement comparison: 1/16 = 0.0625 exactly.
print("with replacement, (13/52)^2:", (13/52) ^ 2)

// Drawing without replacement also changes the ace count: after one ace
// is drawn only 3 of the 51 cards left are aces.
print("P(second card is an ace | first was an ace):", 3/51)
print("P(second card is an ace | first was not):", 4/51)
// ---- expected output ----
// = ncr count: ncr(4, 2) / ncr(52, 2) = 1/221
// = product: (4/52) * (3/51) = 1/221
// = true
// = ordered count: (13 * 13) / (52 * 51) = 13/204
// = product: (13/52) * (13/51) = 13/204
// = with replacement, (13/52)^2: 0.0625
// = P(second card is an ace | first was an ace): 1/17
// = P(second card is an ace | first was not): 4/51
